<title>USA: Starrett Corp Q4 net sharply lower.</title>
<headline>Starrett Corp Q4 net sharply lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.04		    $0.56</p>
<p> Net			    309		    3,466</p>
<p> Revs			58,552		   52,350</p>
<p>		     Year</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.70		    $1.18</p>
<p> Net			  4,335		    7,365</p>
<p> Revs		     167,282		  138,837</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   6,261		    6,261</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Income taxes were $2.6 million vs $2.2 million in qtr and $5.8 million vs $5.0 million in year with unusually high 1996 tax rate resulting from repartriation of profits from Puerto Rico.</p>
<p>1995 pre-tax net included $3.0 million refinancing fee.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
